flowchart TD
    A[How Your Brain Learns] --> B[Focused Mode]
    A --> C[Diffuse Mode]
    A --> D[Chunking]
    A --> E[Memory & Sleep]

    B --> B1[Concentrated attention]
    B --> B2[Uses well-worn neural pathways]
    B --> B3[Best for: Applying known formulas]
    B --> B4[Signal to switch: Frustration after 15-20 min]

    C --> C1[Relaxed, big-picture state]
    C --> C2[Default Mode Network active]
    C --> C3[Best for: Making remote associations]
    C --> C4[How to enter: Walk, shower, exercise]

    D --> D1[Working memory: ~4 chunks max]
    D --> D2[Compress info into larger chunks]
    D --> D3[Build chunks through practice]

    E --> E1[Sleep consolidates memories]
    E --> E2[Procedural vs Declarative knowledge]
    E --> E3[Neuroplasticity: brain physically changes]
